# Build context for docker/pipeline.Dockerfile and docker/airflow.Dockerfile.
#
# Both declare `context: .` in docker-compose.yml, so without this file the whole repository
# is sent to the Docker daemon on every build: about 15 MB, of which 4.6 MB is .git and none
# of which any build stage reads beyond four paths.
#
# DENY BY DEFAULT, then allow exactly what a Dockerfile copies. A denylist is the more common
# shape and the weaker one: it protects against the files you thought of, and a new secret
# added later is included by default. With deny-first, a new file has to be named before it can
# reach a build, which is the correct direction for that mistake to fail in.
#
# This also closes a latent leak rather than a hypothetical one. `COPY dbt/ /app/dbt/` is
# unfiltered, so running `make dbt-build` locally and then rebuilding would place dbt/logs/ in
# the image, and a dbt log records the connection profile it used. Nothing is leaking today
# because those directories happen not to exist; that is luck, not a control.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Everything is excluded to begin with. This covers .env and .env.* without
#    naming them, which matters because the generated .env holds live database
#    passwords and sits in the repository root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Allow only the paths a Dockerfile actually reads.
#    pipeline.Dockerfile: requirements/pipeline.txt, ingest/, dbt/
#    airflow.Dockerfile:  requirements/pipeline.txt, dbt/
#    scripts/ is absent on purpose: no Dockerfile copies it and no container reads it.
#    tests/ is deliberately absent: it reaches the containers as a read-only
#    volume mount, not by COPY, so it does not belong in a build context.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!requirements/
!ingest/
!dbt/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Re-exclude generated output inside those allowed trees. Order matters: a
#    later pattern wins, so these override the allow rules above.
#
#    dbt writes target/, logs/ and dbt_packages/ into the project directory. All
#    three are build output, all three are gitignored, and all three would be
#    swept into the image by the unfiltered `COPY dbt/`. logs/ is the one that
#    matters: dbt.log contains the resolved connection profile.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dbt/target/
dbt/logs/
dbt/dbt_packages/
dbt/package-lock.yml.bak

# Python bytecode: never useful in an image, and it invalidates the COPY layer
# cache on every local test run.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Editor and OS noise that would otherwise bust the cache for the copied trees.
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
